PDP-11 shared visitor counter — updated 2026-09-21

PDP-Gary addition — 2026-09-23
  pdp-ai.html has an independent total in the same Caddy database.
  TOTAL VISITS counts Gary browser sessions; ONLINE NOW counts sessions seen
  on Gary in the past 90 seconds. Visible pages heartbeat every 30 seconds.
  Hashed random session tokens expire after 24 hours of inactivity. No IPs or
  chats are recorded. See config/README.varnish.md for deployment and semantics.

The following describes the original homepage counter:

Display: VISITORS: n in the masthead.
Count: approximate browser sessions, not unique people.
One increment per browser-session cookie, with sessionStorage as fallback.
Reloads and TMOG-11 snapshot refreshes never increment. Blocked storage: read only.
Different browsers and hostnames can count separately. JavaScript is needed.
The marker is reserved before sending the request: interrupted visits may be
missed. Simultaneous first loads in different tabs may race. No identity/IP
list is stored. Direct calls can increment: this is not fraud-resistant analytics.

The authoritative total is now on caddy (192.168.1.45), independent of the
selected PDP. Source/configuration and restore steps: config/README.varnish.md.

Linux:
  /usr/local/libexec/pdp-visitors.py          Python standard-library service
  /etc/systemd/system/pdp-visitors.service   starts on boot
  /var/lib/pdp-visitors/visitors.sqlite       persistent SQLite total
  127.0.0.1:6083                             loopback only

PDP (both .26 and .29):
  /usr/src/local/webtop/visit-proxy.c         integer-only native source
  /home/www/cgi-bin/visit                    forwards one increment to caddy
  /home/www/cgi-bin/visit-total              forwards a read to caddy

Build with make visit-proxy visit-total-proxy. Install only after the proxy
routes counters centrally. Both native helpers use fixed .45:80 and public
Host header; ten-second lifetime, no input and no retry. They run unprivileged.
The existing httpd and inetd need no changes.

Public /visits.txt and /cgi-bin/visit-total are read-only; GET /cgi-bin/visit
increments, HEAD does not. All bypass caches. Transactions serialize updates;
SQLite synchronous=FULL commits durable state. Missing/corrupt state returns
503 instead of resetting to zero. Initialization refuses an existing file.
The fixed-width response contains ten digits and a newline; the page formats it.

The old /home/www-visits/total and /home/www/visits.txt symlink on each PDP are
retained as rollback archives; they are no longer the live count. The old
visit-counter.c remains available for historical restoration.

Back up the live database using the service's backup command and copy it off
caddy. Never reset the total during website deployment. Git stores sources,
not future counter updates. See config/README.varnish.md for backup/restore.
